  "id": "motor-memory",
  "term": "motor memory",
  "definition": "Motor memory is the memory for learned movements or movement patterns. In this historical source, it is illustrated by speech and writing: a person may still be able to move the tongue, lips, hand, or arm, yet lose the remembered co-ordinated acts needed to articulate words or form letters.",
